<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Daily Briefing data seam in Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components</title>
    <phase>0 Removal, prerequisites and seams</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .tsx/.ts code in a shared component consumed by the Console, the standalone page and the SpaarkeAi host; tags include react and frontend</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single-component refactor with explicit defaults and a reference pattern (spaarke-decisions App.tsx injected services); consumers must stay unchanged</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/** only; no BFF or other client files</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, frontend, fluent-ui, refactoring</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Give DailyBriefingApp an injected data service and an injected navigation handler, defaulting to today's authenticatedFetch and Xrm behaviour, so the same component can render inside a sandboxed MCP widget (no network, no MSAL, no Xrm) while the Console, the standalone DailyBriefing page and the SpaarkeAi host keep working unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React 19, Fluent UI v9 and dependency-injected data seams.</role>
  <goal>DailyBriefingAppProps accepts an optional data service (briefing render/narrate/summary and preferences) and an optional navigation handler (open record, open URL, browse playbooks); actions with no injected handler are hidden; with no props supplied the component behaves exactly as today and every existing test passes unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-16 ("DailyBriefingApp gains an injected data service; the Console and the standalone page keep working unchanged, and Xrm navigation becomes an injected handler") and FR-09 (owner: AI Daily Briefing). Reuse scan row "Daily Briefing component": DailyBriefingApp.tsx:75 imports authenticatedFetch (used at ~:895-949); Xrm via getXrm at ~:340, :534, :611; services/briefingService.ts:31 calls authenticatedFetch. Consumers: src/solutions/DailyBriefing/src/main.tsx, src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/dailyBriefing/dailyBriefing.registration.ts, src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/main.tsx (not edited). Task 034 builds the widget on this seam and decides which briefing call the tool returns (spec Unresolved Question).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/components/DailyBriefingApp.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/services/briefingService.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/hooks/useBriefingRender.ts, useBriefingPreferences.ts (accept the injected service)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/services/briefingDataService.ts (interface BriefingDataService + createDefaultBriefingDataService wrapping today's calls)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/index.ts (export the interface and default factory)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/DailyBriefingApp.injectedSeam.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/App.tsx:38 (widget-side injected services)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/worklistService.ts:350 (createWorklistService({ fetch }) injected transport)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">The seam lives in the existing package Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components; no new package. The package stays free of Xrm globals in the injected path and free of any MCP SDK dependency.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Defaults preserve behaviour: with no injected service/handler, the component makes exactly today's calls and navigations; every existing test under src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/ passes without modification, and the three consumers compile without edits.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">When a data service is injected, the component never calls authenticatedFetch, getXrm or window.Xrm for data or navigation (a test asserts it with both spied); interactive actions that need a capability the host did not inject (inline to-do create, email share, dismiss, preferences save) are hidden, not broken.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">No visual change: the injected path renders the same Fluent v9 components with semantic tokens; mirror the existing DigestHeader/TldrSection rendering exactly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund (not npm ci) if dependencies are needed; npm test in the package must pass.</constraint>
  </constraints>

