  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory every network and Xrm call reachable from DailyBriefingApp (component, hooks, services) and list them in the task notes with file:line.</step>
    <step order="2">Define BriefingDataService and a navigation handler type; implement createDefaultBriefingDataService over today's calls; thread both through DailyBriefingApp and the hooks with defaults.</step>
    <step order="3">Hide host-unsupported actions when their capability is not injected.</step>
    <step order="4">Write DailyBriefingApp.injectedSeam.test.tsx; run npm test in the package; type-check the three consumers (tsc --noEmit in src/solutions/DailyBriefing and src/solutions/LegalWorkspace).</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If keeping the default path byte-for-byte requires editing a consumer under src/solutions/**, STOP and escalate (hot-path declaration says SpaarkeAi N).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Daily Briefing component": DailyBriefingApp.tsx:75 and services/briefingService.ts:31 call authenticatedFetch and Xrm directly; verdict "Extend: add a data seam". CAPABILITY-INDEX: no Daily Briefing seam row.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended in place: an optional interface and a default factory inside the existing package; no new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The briefing cannot render in a Copilot widget (the sandbox has no network, MSAL or Xrm), so FR-09/FR-16's Daily Briefing widget (task 034) fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Console briefing unchanged">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=webresource&amp;webResourceName=sprk_spaarkeai</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open the Spaarke Console and the Daily Briefing section</step>
        <step>Verify TL;DR, channel sections and stat tiles render as before</step>
        <step>Open a record link from a briefing row; verify the record modal opens</step>
        <step>Check the console for JavaScript errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Briefing renders and navigates exactly as before the change, with no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Standalone Daily Briefing page unchanged">
      <steps>
        <step>Open the standalone DailyBriefing code page</step>
        <step>Verify render, Browse Playbooks and email share still work</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No behaviour change</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host to dark mode</step>
        <step>Verify backgrounds and text adapt; no hard-coded white or black</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours use Fluent v9 semantic tokens</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">npm test in src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components; tsc --noEmit in consumers</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/services/briefingDataService.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/components/DailyBriefingApp.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/DailyBriefingApp.injectedSeam.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every existing test in Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components passes without modification.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">tsc --noEmit passes in src/solutions/DailyBriefing and src/solutions/LegalWorkspace with no consumer edits.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With an injected data service and navigation handler, the component renders a fixture briefing and makes zero authenticatedFetch, getXrm or window.Xrm calls (spied).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With an injected service but no to-do/email/dismiss capability, those actions are not rendered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: when the injected service rejects, the component shows its existing failed-sections/empty state, not an unhandled error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-16, FR-09. No BFF change. Completed 2026-11-25: BriefingDataService + BriefingNavigationHandler seam (briefingDataService.ts), optional dataService/navigation props on DailyBriefingApp, injected-service args on useBriefingRender/useBriefingPreferences, optional To Do/dismiss on NarrativeBullet and ActivityNotesSection. 11 new tests; package suite 180 -> 191 tests, existing tests unmodified. Inventory, decisions and the test-environment note are in notes/010-decisions.md. Consumer tsc (DailyBriefing, LegalWorkspace) not run here: no node_modules or built dist in the worktree. Out-of-scope findings: none new. rework: none task 010</notes>

